Subject: a simulated loss burst ends in time on a quiet flow
Why: Quiver's simulation of its persisted class (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 6, AC-T2.2.5): stepped per datagram alone, a flow that sent rarely stayed in a loss burst for as long as it sent little, and a restarted publisher's QUIC handshake to its leader met one burst for 30 s (seeds 6302 and 7452); offered upstream on cp/t2.2-told (5b13b2b)

